2. MANUSCRIPTS, FIGURES, TABLES AND RESULTS — CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything under manuscript/, docs/, results/, version_one/manuscript/ and
version_one/results/, and this README.

Copyright (c) 2026 Vahhab Piranfar, licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0).
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt this material for any purpose, including commercially,
provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if
changes were made.

CC BY 4.0 is chosen deliberately rather than a more restrictive Creative Commons
variant. The American Society for Microbiology requires that a repository
carrying code behind a submitted manuscript be licensed no more restrictively
than CC BY, and a NonCommercial or NoDerivatives clause here would make this work
unusable for the purpose it argues for: recomputing a published tolerance call
against its own assay floor.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. THIRD-PARTY DATA — each under its depositor's own licence, not mine
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything under data/. None of it was generated here and none of it is mine to
relicense. Every deposit is recorded in data/raw/SOURCES.json and in a
PROVENANCE.json beside the files, with its source, its DOI or accession, its
licence and a redistributable flag.

The deposits reanalysed in the current manuscript are all CC BY 4.0:

  Vijay et al. 2024        eLife 93243, supplementary file 2
  van Wijk et al. 2023     figshare 19766083
  Windels et al. 2024      Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.7550302
  Kaur et al. 2024         figshare 26462791
  Dubey et al. 2026        Nature Communications Source Data

Attribute those to their depositors, not to this repository. If you redistribute
any of them, carry their CC BY attribution.

Some third-party material used by the earlier study in version_one/ is NOT
redistributable — CC BY-NC-ND, subscription, or with no open licence at all — and
its bytes are therefore excluded from this repository by .gitignore. The
provenance and the fetch route are kept so the analysis can still be reproduced
by anyone who obtains the files from the original deposit. data/raw/SOURCES.json
marks each such entry "redistributable": false.
